From 83df3d305fe16d5d49ce891265152b678bbeefeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 20:58:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(tools): launcher that keeps SteamVR Room Setup from
 crashing on Linux/AMD

Room Setup (Unity 5.6) creates a 50x32 image with 7 mip levels; Vulkan allows 6, and Mesa RADV traps (SIGTRAP in Addr2ComputeSurfaceInfo). The VK_LAYER_vrfix_mipclamp layer clamps mipLevels in vkCreateImage/vkCreateImageView and stubs the VK_EXT_debug_utils calls vrclient makes without a NULL check. vr-room-setup also enables SteamVR's envextensions layer with the external memory/semaphore extensions SteamVR adds itself when it launches Room Setup, so a manual launch works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
