From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat: Room page - saved play areas, auto re-apply and
 Room Setup

Folds the standalone vr-zones tool and the Room Setup launcher into the app (Linux; other platforms get stubs):
- save the current play area under a name, apply / rename / delete it, and
  mark one zone as "auto" (same ~/.config/vr-zones/zones.json as vr-zones)
- a watcher started with the app re-applies the auto zone once per SteamVR
  session and after every base station tilt recalibration ("CALIBRATED base"
  in vrserver.txt), which is when the floor and bounds drift
- a button that launches tools/room-setup-fix/vr-room-setup
- helpers are looked up via BSM_VRCHAP_IO / BSM_ROOM_SETUP, next to the
  executable, or in the source tree's tools/

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
